# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Encyclopedia descriptions, batch D."""
DESC_D = {
    "RT": {
        112: "A mass-production mobile suit developed by Anaheim Electronics for the AEUG.\nDeveloped as an evolution of the GM II, improvements to overall performance and the use of Gundarium gamma armor give it combat capability equal to or exceeding the Marasai. Production efficiency is improved by reusing the Rick Dias's beam saber and the GM II's beam rifle.\nWith no specialized equipment, it is easy for ordinary soldiers to handle, and as the AEUG's main mass-production unit, it supported the AEUG and Karaba through the end of the Gryps Conflict.",
        113: "The AEUG's first variable mobile suit, developed by Anaheim Electronics.\nBuilt to verify the transformation mechanism for the Z Project, it has low combat capability and a fragile airframe as a result.\nDeployed aboard the Argama, it was operated by Reccoa and Fa. In the theatrical version, a second unit appears and sees action in various battles.",
        114: "The AEUG's first variable mobile suit, developed by Anaheim Electronics.\nIts performance is unremarkable in mobile suit form, but in mobile armor form it boasts excellent mobility and acceleration, and has been seen using its speed to run circles around enemies.",
        115: "Developed by the Earth Federation Forces after the One Year War, based on the famed MS-06 Zaku II of the former Principality of Zeon.\nThough its cockpit, armor, and sensors have been reinforced, the mix of Federation and Zeon technology leaves it poorly balanced. Its low output is also a drawback, preventing it from operating more than one beam weapon at a time. Even so, its high versatility was recognized, leading to widespread deployment throughout the Federation Forces.\nUnits deployed to the Titans are painted in a green color scheme.",
        116: "Developed by the Earth Federation Forces after the One Year War, based on the famed MS-06 Zaku II of the former Principality of Zeon.\nThough its cockpit, armor, and sensors have been reinforced, the mix of Federation and Zeon technology leaves it poorly balanced. Its low output is also a drawback, preventing it from operating more than one beam weapon at a time. Even so, its high versatility was recognized, leading to widespread deployment throughout the Federation Forces.\nUnits deployed to Federation forces outside the Titans are painted in a blue color scheme.",
        117: "A mobile suit completed when the Earth Federation Forces modified the Galbaldy Alpha, developed by the Principality of Zeon in the closing days of the One Year War.\nAs part of the Gelgoog lineage, it shares visual similarities with that design. Weight reduction has improved its mobility and maneuverability, but since it is based on an older airframe, its base performance is not high. Even so, when Lila piloted it, she showed nimble movement that belied its origins.",
        118: "An evolution of the Hizack developed by Anaheim Electronics and deployed to the Titans.\nIt is the first Zaku-lineage machine to use Gundarium gamma as its armor material, reducing the airframe's weight and making its movements lighter. The generator output, a weak point of the Hizack, has also been improved, allowing it to operate multiple beam weapons simultaneously.",
        119: "A mass-production variable mobile suit developed by Axis.\nIt was originally developed as a combat-capable variable mobile suit based on the Gaza A and Gaza B, which were used for development and construction work. As a result, its mobility and close-combat ability are low, and its basic tactic is long-range volley fire in groups.\nBecause Axis and the Earth Federation Forces briefly allied at one point, it carries designation numbers from both militaries: AMX-003 for Axis and MMT-1 for the Federation.",
        120: "A Gaza C modified for Haman Karn's personal use.\nIt is painted in a color pattern matching the Qubeley.",
        121: "A variable mobile armor developed by the Earth Federation Forces.\nIt is the first machine to enable a mobile suit to fly independently within an atmosphere.\nIn mobile armor form, its shape gives it excellent durability and resistance to enemy fire, along with outstanding aerial combat capability. Its performance in mobile suit form was also excellent, leading to widespread deployment at Federation bases in the TV version. In the theatrical version, however, only the one unit piloted by Bran Bltark appears.",
        122: "A variable mobile armor originally developed for space use but repurposed for high-altitude interception.\nBoth arms are fitted with active thruster units that can freely redirect their thrust, giving it explosive acceleration especially in mobile armor form. However, this comes at the cost of extreme G-forces, making it a machine that only a few pilots - such as the enhanced human Rosamia or the high G-tolerance Yazan - could handle.\nIt is capable of operating within an atmosphere, but its propellant consumption is severe, making long flights impossible without additional boosters. Early production units also suffered from a blind spot in the lower portion of the panoramic screen due to insufficient adjustment.",
        123: "The first mobile armor developed by Paptimus Scirocco aboard the Jupitris.\nBuilt to withstand the gravity of the Jupiter sphere, roughly 40% of the airframe is taken up by boosters and thruster units. With this mass concentrated at the rear in mobile armor form, it displays especially high mobility.\nIt carries powerful built-in armaments, including mega particle cannons integrated with its back thrusters and arm-mounted grenade launchers. It can also transform into mobile suit form for close combat, making it a well-balanced, excellent machine.",
        124: "A variable mobile suit of the Titans, developed under Scirocco's leadership.\nBesides mobile suit and mobile armor forms, it can also fight in an intermediate, half-man half-horse form.\nIt is armed with the powerful Fedayeen Rifle, comparable to a warship's main gun, for long range, and the Movable Frame Claw for close combat, allowing it to fight effectively at any distance.\nThe fact that it drove Kamille's Gundam Mk-II to the brink of destruction speaks to its high performance.",
        125: "A variable mobile suit of the Titans.\nStabilizers throughout its frame give it high mobility, which improves further in mobile armor form. Its simple transformation mechanism allows for flexible responses in combat, and it is also easy to mass-produce.\nIts unique special weapon, the Shock Wire (also called the Snake), delivers powerful electric attacks that damage not only the machine but the pilot as well. The squadron led by Yazan demonstrated high combat effectiveness by coordinating three units together.",
        126: "A variable mobile armor of the Titans.\nIn mobile armor form it has excellent durability and acceleration, and can attack with its huge claw arms. Its performance in mobile suit form, armed with a beam rifle and a diffuse mega particle cannon, is also excellent, allowing it to hold its own in close combat as well.\nThis is the machine Jerid piloted last in the theatrical version, though its color scheme matches Rosamia's personal unit from the TV version (Jerid's original unit was yellow). In the TV version it was developed as a Newtype-exclusive machine, and its psycommu system was later removed so that any pilot could use it.",
        127: "An experimental mobile suit developed by the Titans.\nLarge jet engines on the shoulders and waist allow it to fly independently within an atmosphere. To reduce air resistance during flight, all of its armaments, including beam sabers and mega particle cannons, are built into its arms.\nSwapping its thrusters allows for further increased acceleration and operation in space.",
        128: "The second mobile suit developed by Scirocco aboard the Jupitris.\nA firepower-focused machine, it is intended to operate as part of a three-unit combination together with the reconnaissance-oriented Bolinoak Sammahn and the melee-focused The O. It carries a wide variety of weaponry, including eight Large Missiles, twin beam cannons, a mega particle cannon, and a diffuse beam cannon, and truly shows its worth in anti-ship combat.\nReccoa piloted this machine, and in the final battle she fought a fierce duel against Emma's Gundam Mk-II.",
        129: "A giant variable mobile armor developed at the Murasame Research Institute, a Newtype research facility, and the Earth Federation Forces' first Newtype-exclusive machine.\nIts pilot is Four Murasame, who came from the Murasame Research Institute. The psycommu system, conventionally used only for machine control and weapons management, is also used by her for remote guidance of the unit. Perhaps because of this power, it places an enormous strain on the pilot's mind, producing a side effect that seems to bind the pilot to the machine as if under a curse.\nIt carries triple mega particle cannons, beam cannons, and other weapons throughout its frame, and the sight of it wrapping Hong Kong City in flames with its excessive firepower is nothing short of a black devil made manifest. It is also capable of flight using a Minovsky Craft system, though only in mobile armor form.",
        130: "The third mobile suit developed by Scirocco aboard the Jupitris.\nDesigned for search and reconnaissance, its radome-shaped composite detection system on the head provides advanced information-gathering capability.\nIts combat ability is by no means low either; numerous vernier thrusters throughout its body give it mobility greater than its appearance suggests. Its armaments are distinctive as well, including a beam tomahawk and a shield that can also function as a beam gun.",
        131: "A Newtype-exclusive mobile suit developed by Axis.\nIt was designed on the concept of a mobile suit version of the Elmeth, the mobile armor of the former Principality of Zeon.\nThe Elmeth's greatest feature was its remote attack terminals, the Bits, but their built-in generators made a certain amount of bulk unavoidable. However, the Funnels equipped on the Qubeley use an energy CAP system, achieving considerable downsizing. Psycommu control extends beyond the Funnels to direct control of the machine itself.",
        132: "A large mobile suit developed by Scirocco aboard the Jupitris.\nIts frame is equipped with reaction attitude control systems and rocket motors throughout, and a Bio-Sensor built into the cockpit gives it excellent responsiveness. Despite the sluggish impression its appearance gives, it possesses top-class mobility and maneuverability.\nIts armaments are equally formidable, including a large beam rifle uniquely modified by Scirocco himself, and hip-mounted sub-manipulators (Arms) that wield beam sabers. It can rightly be called one of the strongest mobile suits of the Gryps Conflict.",
        133: "An assault space cruiser serving as the AEUG's flagship.\nModeled after the White Base, which distinguished itself during the One Year War, it was secretly developed by Brigadier General Blex at the colony 'Sweetwater'. It was initially called the White Base II, but was ultimately named the Argama at the whim of its financial backers.\nIts armor is more robust than it appears, and it carries a total of three main cannons at the ship's center and underside, plus two deflection-type mega particle cannons on its lower flanks. Combined with the high command ability of its captain, Bright Noa, it achieved numerous victories.\nIt is equipped with a residential block that generates simulated gravity through centrifugal force by rotating, a sight that can be seen during the opening.",
        134: "A newly built AEUG warship constructed at Amman on the Moon.\nIt is equipped with three mobile suit catapults at the bow and one at the stern, and carries a large number of mobile suits.\nHenken, the first captain of the Argama, commands this ship, and it has performed on par with the Argama under Bright's command.\nIt is said to be one of four Irish-type ships built at Amman, though no other sister ships appear in the theatrical version.",
        135: "An improved version of the cruiser that served as the Earth Federation Forces' mainstay during the One Year War.\nIt has been modified with additional anti-air weaponry and a catapult installed at the bow. This color scheme is the type used by both the Earth Federation Forces and the Titans.",
        136: "A large land-based transport aircraft of the Earth Federation Forces, built even larger than the Principality of Zeon's Gaw attack carrier that inspired it.\nBuilt for the purpose of transporting mobile suits, its structure is dominated by airframe storage space. It can carry not only dozens of mobile suits but also launch and recover small shuttles. It also boasts a range sufficient to circle the Earth twice without refueling.\nIn the TV version, the units used by the Titans were called the Soudri, but in the theatrical version they are simply referred to as the Garuda-class.",
        137: "A heavy cruiser of the Earth Federation Forces and the Titans' main ship type.\nIts hull is characterized by independently sectioned blocks, giving it excellent damage control.\nThe catapult deck at the bow can launch mobile suits both upward and downward, giving it excellent mobile suit deployment capability.",
        138: "A large space battleship secretly developed by the Titans at Gryps. As their flagship, it also stands as a symbol of the Titans.\nIt carries a large number of mobile suits and has numerous catapult decks capable of launching them in a short time. It also boasts excellent anti-ship bombardment capability, equipped with numerous large-caliber, long-range mega particle cannons.\nScirocco initially served as its captain, achieving results such as the capture of Von Braun City on the Moon. It was later given to Basque by Jamitov, who came to view Scirocco as a threat.",
        139: "A space cruiser of Axis.\nAn evolution of the Musai-class cruiser of the former Principality of Zeon, which distinguished itself during the One Year War. Sister ships include the Sandra and the Mindra.",
        140: "A giant battleship built at Axis, serving as the flagship of the remnants of the former Principality of Zeon.\nAn evolution of the Principality of Zeon's Gwazine-class, its great size gives it superior firepower, mobile suit capacity, and personnel accommodation. It was used as a base of operations when Axis returned to the Earth Sphere.",
        141: "A prototype mobile suit developed by Anaheim Electronics for the purpose of mass-producing the Zeta Gundam. Its name is an abbreviation of \"Refined Gundam Zeta.\"\nIts transformation mechanism has been eliminated; instead, it reaches cruising form by combining with a Back Weapon System that envelops the airframe. However, because the system is jettisoned when transforming into mobile suit form, it cannot be re-equipped on the spot once separated, leaving the machine lacking in flexibility.\nIt combines high mobility and firepower, and its performance as a mobile suit is extremely high in its own right. However, its production cost proved too high, and mass production was abandoned. The single completed unit was assigned to Londo Bell, which was pursuing Neo Zeon.",
        142: "A Newtype-exclusive mobile suit developed by Anaheim Electronics at the request of Londo Bell. Its pilot, Amuro Ray, handled its design himself.\nDeveloped by analyzing the performance of Gundams throughout history and incorporating the latest technology, it was completed as an ultra-high-performance machine that belies its rushed production.\nA Psycho Frame built into the area around the cockpit gives it extraordinary mobility and responsiveness. It is also the first Gundam-type mobile suit capable of using the Fin Funnel, a psycommu weapon. These are larger than ordinary funnels, and correspondingly more powerful. Beyond attack use, several units can be linked together to generate an I Field, forming an anti-beam barrier, making them useful for both offense and defense.\nTo prevent Neo Zeon's attempt to drop Axis onto Earth, it fought and won a decisive battle against Char's Sazabi, which was likewise equipped with a Psycho Frame.",
        143: "A mobile suit that emerged from the White Doll, an object enshrined at the foot of Mountain Cycle in the Ingressa territory of Vicinity.\nAt first it had almost no armaments, fighting in melee with its bare hands or a beam saber. Later, a rifle, shield, hammer, and other equipment were excavated, and equipping these steadily improved its combat power.\nIt operates via the I Field Beam Drive (IFBD), which spreads an internally generated I Field across the airframe's surface and controls the machine by manipulating it. Since it carries no generator, its internal structure has ample room to spare, and the Multi-Purpose Silo (a general-purpose weapons cache) installed in its chest can be loaded with a variety of armaments as needed. Loran in fact used it to carry all manner of things, from nuclear missiles to cattle.\nIts nanomachine-coated armor has self-repair capability, and given enough time it can even regenerate missing parts.\nThe Moonlight Butterfly (M-Fly) system, arguably Turn A Gundam's greatest feature, scatters nanomachines carried on an I Field, and is said to have destroyed the scientific civilization of the previous century.\nThe cockpit in the waist can separate and transform into the Core Fighter. It has almost no combat power of its own, but it is an indispensable part for properly using the Moonlight Butterfly system.\nOnly a few characters in the story call it \"Gundam\" - Loran and most others instead call it the 'White Doll' or the 'White Beard.'",
        144: "A mobile suit excavated from Mountain Cycle.\nDeployed in large numbers to the Ingressa Militia, it seems that in many cases pilots from flight squadrons - such as Sochie and Meshe - simply took over as its pilots.\nIn appearance it closely resembles Neo Zeon's AMX-109 Kapool, but judging from the shape of its cockpit and its somewhat smaller airframe, it is believed to be a replica.\nIt saw action surpassing its original, including the use of Turn A Gundam's hammer and, after modification, operation in outer space.",
        145: "A Kapool modified as Corin Nander's personal machine.\nDespite being hastily built, it was more than a match for the Mahiroo and the Bandit, thanks to Corin's skill.\nIt has an overabundance of distinguishing features: a red paint job far from its original color, a large Minchi Drill diverted from an Eagail, a Wodom's severed arm rigged to fire as a Rocket Punch, and finally a set of horn ornaments added to its head.",
        146: "A mobile suit excavated from Mountain Cycle in the Rujanna territory.\nNamed after the local ruler, Duke Borjarno, it was deployed to the Suicide Squad of the Rujanna Militia.\nIn appearance it closely resembles the Principality of Zeon's MS-06 Zaku II (in fact, Rett's unit called it a Zaku), but judging from the shape of its cockpit and its performance, it is believed to be a replica.\nIt is highly versatile, capable of space operation with minor modification, and excelled at group combat using the varied weaponry excavated alongside it.",
        147: "A mobile suit deployed to the Dianna Guard; silver-colored units are ridden by rank-and-file soldiers.\nPoe, though not a member of the Guard, used one as well.",
        148: "A mobile suit deployed to the Dianna Guard; the gold-colored unit is the personal machine of the squad's captain, Harry.\nIt shares many features with Turn A Gundam, including its IFBD, cockpit position, and basic airframe structure.\nBeyond basic armaments like the heat fan and beam gun, an I Field generator mounted on its left hand can neutralize enemy guided weapons and hijack the IFBD control of enemy machines.\nAttaching skirt-shaped aerial maneuvering units to both sides of its waist also enables long-distance flight.",
        149: "A small mobile suit used by the Dianna Counter.\nIt is formally classified as a Walking Dumpling, which is also the origin of its abbreviated name, WaD.\nThough small, it sees remarkably wide use: fighting large mobile suits through group tactics, its original purpose of anti-personnel combat, cargo transport, facility construction, and even excavation work.\nWithin the Militia it was nicknamed the 'Armadillo,' and captured units were used as well.",
        150: "A large anti-ship combat mobile suit of the Dianna Counter.\nIts name is short for Walking Dome, and true to that name, the dome on its head houses an array of weapons, including anti-air Vulcan cannons and an anti-ship beam cannon. Its bombardment is powerful enough to reshape mountains.\nArmor coated in nano-skin gives it self-repair capability, and it excels in both firepower and armor. However, its huge frame and heavy armament leave it weak in close combat, as shown when Turn A Gundam severed its wrist with a hand chop.\nWithin the Militia it was nicknamed the 'Scarecrow.'",
        151: "A Wodom painted red. It is operated by a unit stationed at the mass-driver system 'Sacktrager', used to launch objects from the ground into space.",
        152: "A melee-focused mobile suit excavated from Mountain Cycle on the Moon and independently modified by Corin. Its main armament is the Minchi Drill, likewise modified by Corin from civilian excavation heavy machinery.\nMaking use of a spine structure running from head to tail, it can transform into a high-speed walking form reminiscent of a dinosaur. In this form, it can deliver headbutts using its head like a blunt weapon.",
        153: "The main mobile suit of the Ghingnham fleet.\nIn addition to the overwhelming firepower of the mega particle cannon built into its toroidal shield-mounted right shoulder, it possesses excellent aerial combat ability and mobility, surpassing the SUMO in overall performance.\nIt is the only machine with an artificial muscle-fiber drive system, and it is speculated that it was originally equipped with a 'Mobile Trace System' that captured the pilot's myoelectric signals and fed them back into the machine's movements.",
        154: "A mobile suit excavated from Mountain Cycle on the Moon.\nSeveral units were excavated, but aside from the one piloted by Merribeth, the rest are unmanned drones that move in coordination with it.\nIt possesses unique armaments, including Oozy Armor (secretion armor) that hardens nanomachines to improve bullet resistance, and a group of Squeeze Weapons designed to destroy enemy machines without killing their pilots. Because of this, it truly shows its worth in anti-mobile-suit combat.\nIt is also unusual in having a cockpit designed to be operated while standing.",
        155: "A mobile suit excavated from Mountain Cycle on the Moon.\nCalled a Turn-type machine like Turn A Gundam, the two cause a resonance phenomenon when they sense each other's presence.\nUnlike Turn A Gundam, its cockpit is located in the head, allowing it to function independently. It can also separate its entire body into nine parts to perform all-range attacks, and can restrain enemies to steal their data. Through this ability it absorbed Turn A Gundam's data, gaining the ability to use the Moonlight Butterfly (M-Fly) as well.\nIt has a nanomachine-based self-repair function, but an X-shaped scar on its chest, said to have been inflicted by Turn A Gundam in the past, remains to this day for reasons unknown.\nThe origin of the name 'X' is said to mean 'that which had its path bent by the tenth (X) star.'",
        156: "The flagship used by the Dianna Counter during its operation to return to Earth.\nBecause it also serves as the mobile royal palace of Dianna, the Moon's queen, its appearance is far more beautiful than one would expect of a warship. However, it possesses more defensive power than its looks suggest, including a powerful I Field.\nThe bow section can also separate to operate as a mobile command post.",
        157: "A warship used by the Dianna Counter during its operation to return to Earth.\nIt is equipped with a giant beam saber generated at the front of the hull for storming enemy bases, as well as an anti-ship main cannon on its upper deck.",
        158: "A mobile suit developed by the former Federation Forces during the Seventh Space War.\nWith its Flash System, capable of controlling bit mobile suits, and its Satellite Cannon, powerful enough to destroy a colony, it becomes the strongest weapon of all in the hands of a Newtype pilot.\nThe unit piloted by Garrod is one of several produced. Unlike the Gundam Airmaster and Gundam Leopard developed around the same time, it requires a G Controller - doubling as both the right control lever and the Satellite Cannon's firing trigger - to be attached before it can be activated.",
        159: "A machine reinforced and modified by Kid, using \"some amazing parts he'd kept in reserve,\" to compensate for the firepower shortfall of the Gundam X after its Satellite Cannon was destroyed in the battle with the Vertigo.\nThough it has lost the Satellite Cannon, equipping the Divider for which it is named allows it to maintain stable performance even without the moon in the sky.\nThe Divider, also known as the Harmonica Cannon, combines the functions of a multi-barrel beam cannon, a deployable shield, and propulsion verniers. It is a versatile weapon that provides a range of benefits, from offense and defense to improved mobility.",
        160: "A machine reinforced and modified from the Gundam Airmaster after it was heavily damaged in battle with the New Federation Forces. It is the crystallization of facilities and materials provided by General Lee of the Republic of Estard, combined with the ideas and skill of Kid, who was \"moved\" by seeing them.\nAt a glance, the change in the machine's color from red to blue draws the most attention, but this refit actually focuses on improving the firepower that was the Airmaster's greatest weakness. In particular, replacing the nose Vulcan with a beam cannon allows it to display high combat power in flight mode.\nLarge boosters at the wingtips also improved its thrust, to the point that it can now carry the Gundam Leopard riding on top while flying, whereas before it had to carry it by lifting it.\nBy design, combining with the G Falcon could theoretically produce output exceeding that of a cruiser-class warship, but this was never put to use in actual combat.",
        161: "A machine that was actually reinforced and modified after Kid, upon seeing the Gundam Leopard heavily damaged in battle with the New Federation Forces, declared, \"A full overhaul would be faster than fixing it.\"\nThe machine's color was changed from green to a red-based scheme, further boosting its already high firepower.\nMany of its originally solid-round-heavy weapons were replaced with beam weapons. In particular, the inner-arm gatling gun on its right arm was replaced with twin beam cylinders mounted on both arms, converting it from a solid-round weapon to a beam weapon and doubling the number of barrels, resulting in more than twice its effective firepower.\nCombining with the G Falcon finally made possible the aerial operation Roybea had long wished for. However, the battlefield shifted to space immediately afterward, so it was never put to use in actual combat.",
    },
}
